# <<< dotfiles-managed gitignore <<<

# Project-specific overrides. Placed AFTER the managed block on purpose:
# gitignore uses last-match-wins, so negating a rule defined inside the
# block above only works below it — re-running .dotfiles.sh only touches
# the text between the markers, never this section.

# The managed block's `screenshot-*.png` / `screenshot-*.jpg` rule (E2E Test
# & Browser Artifacts) targets Playwright's own failure-screenshot dumps, but
# the glob has no path scope, so it was also silently keeping PinchGrab's
# Chrome Web Store listing screenshots out of version control entirely
# (PGRB-001) — un-ignore them explicitly.
!store-assets/screenshot-*.png

# Public-surface cut: internal orchestration machinery removed from the public
# tree. The dotfiles-managed block above force-includes some of these paths, so
# re-ignore them here (last-match-wins) to keep any dotfiles re-stamp local
# instead of letting it re-commit into the public repo.
/lib/composio-orchestrator/
/lib/symphony-elixir/
/bin/symphony
/WORKFLOW.md
/.symphony/
/old/
